\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, I know that all my life
\par Is portioned out for me,
\par And the changes that are sure to come
\par I do not fear to see;
\par But I ask Thee for a present mind,
\par Intent on pleasing Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I ask Thee for a thoughtful love,
\par Through constant watching wise,
\par To meet the glad with joyful smiles,
\par And wipe the weeping eyes,
\par And a heart at leisure from itself
\par To soothe and sympathize.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I would not have the restless will
\par That hurries to and fro,
\par Seeking for some great thing to do
\par Or secret thing to know;
\par I would be treated as a child,
\par And guided where I go.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Wherever in the world I am,
\par In whatsoe'er estate,
\par I have a fellowship with hearts
\par To keep and cultivate,
\par And a work of lowly love to do
\par For the Lord on whom I wait.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I ask Thee for the daily strength
\par To none that ask denied,
\par And a mind to blend with outward life,
\par Still keeping at Thy side,
\par Content to fill a little space
\par If Thou be glorified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. In a service which Thy will appoints
\par There are no bonds for me;
\par For my inmost soul is taught the truth
\par That makes Thy children free;
\par And a life of self-renouncing love 
\par Is a life of liberty.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

